   little worth compiling; what is worth compiling is the instruct chain they build -- the
   new road's jitter walk (S0-S6, "a walk over the finished chain"). If so, the rule door is a
   bridge, not the destination: chains compiled op by op, one emitter per operator, instead
   of rule actions compiled one at a time. To be measured as the road goes, rule by rule.

